{"tool_name":"htsanalyzer","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"htsanalyzer","home":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/HTSanalyzeR.html","license":"Artistic-2.0","summary":"This package provides classes and methods for gene set over-representation, enrichment and network analyses on high-throughput screens. A pipeline is also specifically designed for cellHTS2 object to perform integrative network analyses of high-throughput RNA interference screens. The users can build their own analysis pipeline for their own data set based on this package.","addition_date":"2017-01-17T14:59:31Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-30T15:42:20Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["2.26.0"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:htsanalyzer","credit":[{"email":"xinwang2hms@gmail.com","name":"Xin Wang","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-5122-2418","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/HTSanalyzeR.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Gene expression data","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2603"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]},{"data":{"term":"ID list","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2872"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]},{"data":{"term":"Pathway or network","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2600"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Gene set testing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3224"},{"term":"Gene to pathway mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0533"},{"term":"Gene-set enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2436"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"P-value","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1669"},"format":[{"term":"HTML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2331"},{"term":"Image format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3547"},{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]},{"data":{"term":"Plot","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2884"},"format":[{"term":"HTML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2331"},{"term":"Image format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3547"},{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]},{"data":{"term":"Report","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2048"},"format":[{"term":"HTML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2331"},{"term":"Image format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3547"},{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]}]}],"name":"HTSanalyzeR","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"bioconductor_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btr028","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: High-throughput screens (HTS) by RNAi or small molecules are among the most promising tools in functional genomics. They enable researchers to observe detailed reactions to experimental perturbations on a genome-wide scale. While there is a core set of computational approaches used in many publications to analyze these data, a specialized software combining them and making them easily accessible has so far been missing. Results: Here we describe HTSanalyzeR, a flexible software to build integrated analysis pipelines for HTS data that contains over-representation analysis, gene set enrichment analysis, comparative gene set analysis and rich sub-network identification. HTSanalyzeR interfaces with commonly used pre-processing packages for HTS data and presents its results as HTML pages and network plots. \u00a9 The Author(s) 2011. Published by Oxford University Press.","authors":[{"name":"Markowetz F."},{"name":"Rose J.C."},{"name":"Terfve C."},{"name":"Wang X."}],"citationCount":81,"date":"2011-03-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"